# Alpha Admin design system (agents)

Canonical product write-up: `../alpha-docs/ADR-shared-design-system.md` (esp. §3 / §3b).

## Accent

- Accent is a **whisper** for checks, sparse marks, focus — **not** selected cards, section rows, FABs, body text, or primary CTAs.
- Never paint selected Settings cards / list rows with accent border or accent wash. Use grayscale fill (`--fg-4` / `--fg-8`).
- Alpha default / Admin / Niel: **three** accents — `--accent-1` blurple (success/checks), `--accent-2` gold (in-progress / Sending… / Publishing…), `--accent-3` rouge (urgency marks + destructive icons). Customer sites may still derive companions from one brand accent.

## Feed / list rows (2nd column)

- **Selected** = `var(--fg-4)` only (same as Tasks / Projects / `app.css` `.feed .row.on`). Never `--fg-8` for selected cards.
- **Title** 14px / 600 / `--fg`; **timestamp** 12px / 500 / `--fg-33` with ≥2px trailing pad (prefer preview-row trail).
- **Preview:** Chat message line `--fg-66`; Notes body snippet quieter `--fg-33`. People on the right via `ProfilePic` / `ProfilePicStack`.
- Chat stacking: publication panels are barriers (`chat-stack.js`). See ADR §3c.
- **Empty:** large centered muted copy like Chat (`empty-title` ~1.65rem / `--fg-33`, `empty-body` 14px / `--fg-16`) — not small left-aligned list chrome.

## Typography

- **NEVER use monospace for anything** — not counts, timestamps, codes in chrome, seen-by receipts, or overlays. No `font-family: monospace`, no `ui-monospace` / `Menlo` stacks, no `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` / `tabular` figure tricks for UI counts. Use the same Inter / `--font-sans` body type as surrounding labels.

## Icons

- Prefer existing icons: `Pen`, `Share` (filled), `Crown`, `Trash`, `Folder`, `NavIcon`, `@alpha/ui` SVGs.
- Do **not** invent inline person/share glyphs when a product icon exists.
- Icon color on quiet chrome: `currentColor` at `--fg-66`, not full ink.
- Selected nav pills use `icons/{name}.png` via `navPngUrl` (Chat → `chat.png`, Files → `folder.png`). Inactive = stroke `NavIcon` / `Folder.svelte`.

## Buttons

- Default chrome actions: **pill / round** with subtle `--fg-8` background, no heavy stroke.
- Avoid stroked rectangular buttons inside cards.
- Primary CTAs: ink-on-bg (existing `--button-primary-*`), not accent-filled.

## Modals / sheets

- **Never** show a visual drag handle / grabber pill on Modal, CreateSheet, or generic bottom sheets — not on mobile, not on desktop.
- Shared top chrome (`SheetTopbar`): close **X** (left) + centered title + trailing. Desktop 28 glass / 14px title; mobile 44 round / **17px** title (match `ChromeMobileBar`). Create sheets: **no** SheetTopbar row — content owns title/actions (overlay / Escape / drag-dismiss). Nav Create/Search still use Modal + SheetTopbar. Chrome icon pills: **scale only** on hover — no color wash.
- **Exception — comment panels:** X + centered “Comments” + `Drag` grabber (right) for resize / drag-under-min dismiss. Same pattern in Admin `CommentThread` and public `CommentSection`.
- Comment FAB ↔ panel morph: fixed `--comments-radius` per breakpoint so only width/height animate — never transition `border-radius`. Desktop: **22px** (half of 44px FAB) on the full rounded floating card; mobile: `--radius-hero` (**34px**) top radii only.
- Mobile modal/sheet top radii: `--radius-hero` (34px) concentric with round chrome buttons (12 pad + 22). Desktop cards: `calc(var(--radius-hero) - 2px)`, centered.
- Mobile sheets may still support drag-down-to-dismiss as a gesture.
- Comment / chat entity panels: FAB inset inside the detail column (`~20px`); open panel matches Modal glass (`--modal-bg` / `--glass-panel`). Desktop floating card keeps **full** rounded corners (incl. bottom). Composer chrome matches Chat (`ChatComposer` + quote bar).

## Mobile scrollbars

- ≤767px: **no scrollbars by default** (`@alpha/ui/scrollbars.css`) — overflow still scrolls.
- Opt in with `.show-scrollbar` only when scroll affordance is otherwise unclear.
- Do **not** opt in for horizontal emoji rows, pill tracks, or segmented controls (stay hidden).

## Horizontal scroll vs page swipe

- Any overflow-x row (reactions emoji strip, attach pill track, SegmentedControl, …) must mark **`data-h-scroll`**.
- That attribute: `touch-action: pan-x` + `overscroll-behavior-x: contain` (via `scrollbars.css`), and UiShell / DetailColumn **exclude** it from nav-open / swipe-back so row scroll wins over page gestures.
- Prefer this shared marker over one-off `stopPropagation` / per-surface gesture forks.

## Popovers

Canonical surface + rows: `@alpha/ui/popover.css` (`.alpha-popover`, `.alpha-popover-list`, `.alpha-popover-item`, `.alpha-popover-ico`). FloatPanel / DropdownMenu / chat actions / in-flow menus share this chrome.

- **Glass:** `--composer-bg` / `--modal-bg` + specular hairline (same as scroll-FAB) — do not invent new fills.
- **No outer vertical padding** on the item column — tight to first/last rows (`padding: 0` on `.alpha-popover-list`).
- **Icon before every item** in a plain square `.alpha-popover-ico` (sizing only — no bg/border/radius). Icons fit width **or** height of the square. Missing glyph → `ChevronRight`.
- **Labels muted** (`--fg-66`) — never full `--fg`, including hover/active.
- **Destructive** menu actions → `--accent-3` / `--destructive` (rouge). Not Settings Disconnect grayscale.
- **Anchor:** chrome triggers → element `anchor`; context menus (Mail inbox, etc.) → `point` `{ x: clientX, y: clientY }` so the panel opens at the tap/pointer — never “below the whole card” by default.
- **Chat bubble actions:** transparent dismiss scrim (no modal wash); reactions pill stays its own glass panel; actions list = standard popover rows. Plus overlays the reactions row (fade mask; row scrolls underneath). Expanding reactions morphs the **same** pill in place (width/height only, fixed `--reactions-radius` — never transition radius; no second overlay panel).

## Destructive

- Settings Disconnect / cancel-danger chrome: **grayscale only** (muted text + quiet fill).
- Delete / trash / urgency icons + marks: use `--accent-3` / `--destructive` (rouge).
- In-progress indicators (task boxes, Sending…, Publishing…): `--accent-2` (gold) — never rouge.

## Settings profiles

- No duplicate “Profiles” header under the shell Settings title.
- Admin = **crown** beside name; do not print owner/admin/member labels on cards.
- Cards use **Modal glass** (`--modal-bg` / `--glass-panel` + `--glass-blur` + `--glass-border`) — not `--fg-4` wash. Selected card slightly larger; same quiet stroke as unselected + Add.
- Collapsed hub: **real** card stack — selected on top, max **two** other profile cards underneath (lower opacity + more scale-down each). Stack display gets **+8px** L/R pad.
- Expand (chevronDown): cards **morph continuously** from under the stack (margin + scale — no staggered pop-in); animate hub sections away so the deck owns the page. Chevron → glass **Select** pill on every profile card.
- Last card = **Add a Profile** — leading glass `+` (same size as PFPs), quieter label (`--fg-66`), same glass stroke as other cards. Scale-only hover — no color washes.
- Detail chrome: round icon pills (Pen, filled Share) — not text CTAs.
